didunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua. Ut enim ad minim veniam, quis nostrud exercitation tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua. Ut enim ad minim veniam, quis nostrud exercitation.\"),\"content\",\"\"),\"url\",\"https://uat.icg.citi.com/icghome/what-we-think/speakers/ken-porcaro\"),\"bios\",\"\u003cp\u003eDiane Arber is a Managing Director and Head of Human Resources for Citi's Institutional Clients Group (ICG). In this capacity, she oversees Human Resources for Markets and Securities Services, Banking Capital Markets and Advisory, Treasury and Trade Solutions, Citi Private Bank and ICG Operations and Technology. Within these business lines, Diane is responsible for the strategy and execution of all Human Resources objectives including talent development and succession planning, retention, compensation and diversity.\u003c/p\u003e\\n\u003cp\u003eIn addition to her role within ICG, Diane is also Senior Human Resources Officer responsible for Human Resources Professional Services (HRPS), Canada and Japan\u0026rsquo;s Human Resources divisions. She is a member of Citi\u0026rsquo;s Human Resources Operating Committee and the Institutional Client Group\u0026rsquo;s Leadership Team.\u003c/p\u003e\\n\u003cp\u003eShe began her career at a predecessor firm Salomon Brothers in 1990 as a Human Resources Analyst. During her 29 years of service at Citi, Diane has held a number of senior Human Resources positions in both New York and London prior to being appointed to her current position.\u003c/p\u003e\\n\u003cp\u003eDiane serves on the Board of The Center for Anti-Violence Education, a non-profit organization dedicated to the development and implementation of comprehensive violence prevention programs for individuals and organizations, providing underserved communities throughout the New York metropolitan area with skills to break cycles of violence\u003c/p\u003e\\n\u003cp\u003e--\u003c/p\u003e\\n\u003cp\u003eDiane Arber is a Managing Director and Head of Human Resources for Citi's Institutional Clients Group (ICG). In this capacity, she oversees Human Resources for Markets and Securities Services, Banking Capital Markets and Advisory, Treasury and Trade Solutions, Citi Private Bank and ICG Operations and Technology. Within these business lines, Diane is responsible for the strategy and execution of all Human Resources objectives including talent development and succession planning, retention, compensation and diversity.\u003c/p\u003e\\n\u003cp\u003eIn addition to her role within ICG, Diane is also Senior Human Resources Officer responsible for Human Resources Professional Services (HRPS), Canada and Japan\u0026rsquo;s Human Resources divisions. She is a member of Citi\u0026rsquo;s Human Resources Operating Committee and the Institutional Client Group\u0026rsquo;s Leadership Team.\u003c/p\u003e\\n\u003cp\u003eShe began her career at a predecessor firm Salomon Brothers in 1990 as a Human Resources Analyst. During her 29 years of service at Citi, Diane has held a number of senior Human Resources positions in both New York and London prior to being appointed to her current position.\u003c/p\u003e\\n\u003cp\u003eDiane serves on the Board of The Center for Anti-Violence Education, a non-profit organization dedicated to the development and implementation of comprehensive violence prevention programs for individuals and organizations, providing underserved communities throughout the New York metropolitan area with skills to break cycles of violence\u003c/p\u003e\\n\u003cp\u003eDiane Arber is a Managing Director and Head of Human Resources for Citi's Institutional Clients Group (ICG). In this capacity, she oversees Human Resources for Markets and Securities Services, Banking Capital Markets and Advisory, Treasury and Trade Solutions, Citi Private Bank and ICG Operations and Technology. Within these business lines, Diane is responsible for the strategy and execution of all Human Resources objectives including talent development and succession planning, retention, compensation and diversity.\u003c/p\u003e\\n\u003cp\u003eIn addition to her role within ICG, Diane is also Senior Human Resources Officer responsible for Human Resources Professional Services (HRPS), Canada and Japan\u0026rsquo;s Human Resources divisions. She is a member of Citi\u0026rsquo;s Human Resources Operating Committee and the Institutional Client Group\u0026rsquo;s Leadership Team.\u003c/p\u003e\\n\u003cp\u003eShe began her career at a predecessor firm Salomon Brothers in 1990 as a Human Resources Analyst. During her 29 years of service at Citi, Diane has held a number of senior Human Resources positions in both New York and London prior to being appointed to her current position.\u003c/p\u003e\\n\u003cp\u003eDiane serves on the Board of The Center for Anti-Violence Education, a non-profit organization dedicated to the development and implementation of comprehensive violence prevention programs for individuals and organizations, providing underserved communities throughout the New York metropolitan area with skills to break cycles of violence\u003c/p\u003e\"),\"presentationTime\",\"12 Oct 2021, 14:00 GMT\"),\"linkedin\",\"https://www.wikihow.com/Create-an-Email-Link-in-HTML\"),\"email\",\"wanting.xu@citi.com\")},5150:function(e){e.exports=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\"},5220:function(e,t,r){\"use strict\";r.d(t,{default:function(){return E}});var n=r(2284),i=r(4467),o=r(3453),a=r(4883),c=r.n(a),l=r(9917),s=r.n(l),u=r(5241),d=r(2581),m=r(8274),f=r(7715),g=r(8180),p={title:\"\",summary:\"\",defaultImage:\"\",thumbnailImage:\"\",videoLink:\"\",clientCategory:\"\",category:\"\",id:\"\",insightType:\"\",clientBusinessType:\"\",relatedType:\"\",destinationLink:\"\",publishDate:\"\",url:\"\",image:\"\",topic:\"\",bcmaTags:\"\"},A=r(491),y=r(1808),h=r(8600),_=r(9610);function M(e,t){var r=Object.keys(e);if(Object.getOwnPropertySymbols){var n=Object.getOwnPropertySymbols(e);t\u0026\u0026(n=n.filter(function(t){return Object.getOwnPro